.TH "FLOX\-BUILD\-UPDATE\-CATALOGS" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-build\-update\-catalogs \- Update catalog lockfile for Nix
expression builds
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general\-options>] build update\-catalogs
     [\-d=<path>]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the catalog configuration from \f[CR].flox/nix\-builds.toml\f[R]
and generate (or regenerate) the lockfile at
\f[CR].flox/nix\-builds.lock\f[R].
.PP
Each catalog entry in \f[B]\f[CB]nix\-builds.toml(5)\f[B]\f[R] is
resolved and pinned: Nix source\-type catalogs are locked with
\f[CR]nix flake prefetch\f[R], and FloxHub catalogs are locked against
the FloxHub API.
The resulting lockfile pins every catalog to a specific revision,
ensuring reproducible builds.
.PP
Both \f[CR].flox/nix\-builds.toml\f[R] and
\f[CR].flox/nix\-builds.lock\f[R] should be committed to version control
so that all collaborators build against identical catalog inputs.
.PP
This command only works with path (local) environments.
It cannot be used with managed or remote environments.
.PP
If no \f[CR].flox/nix\-builds.toml\f[R] file exists, the command prints
a warning with the expected file path and exits without error.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Environment Options
If no environment is specified for an environment command, the
environment in the current directory or the active environment that was
last activated is used.
.TP
\f[CR]\-d\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R]
Path containing a .flox/ directory.
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
